course: dictionary
lesson: 6289
title: Reading the mood of a word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe a feeling, and the words around them show which feeling. «Moody» can mean a person who keeps changing mood, or someone who is grumpy right now. The rest of the sentence tells you which meaning is meant.
explain: Look for clues. «Skipping meals leaves them tired, moody and slower» shows that moody is linked to tiredness and being hungry, so it means grumpy or cross, not happy. Ask yourself: does my meaning fit the feeling of the whole sentence?
explain: Moody can also describe things that are not people. A moody painting or moody lighting is dark and gloomy, and it makes you feel mysterious or sad. The clue is the word it describes: a painting cannot be grumpy, so moody must mean something else.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Moody» can mean often changing mood, grumpy or sulky right now, or dark and gloomy in a way that creates a feeling.
fact: «Mardy» means moody and grumpy, as in «Mind your own, mardy».
fact: «Threenager» is a jokey word for a defiant three-year-old acting like a moody teenager.
fact: Growing children need regular meals, because skipping meals can leave them tired, moody and grumpy.
exercise: Dad is moody today and won't talk to anyone. What does moody mean here? | *Grumpy and sulky right now | Happy and bouncy | Made of wood | Very hungry
exercise: «The moody painting showed a dark sky over a lonely sea.» What does moody mean? | Bright and cheerful | Loud and noisy | *Dark and gloomy, creating a feeling | Very large
exercise: «Skipping meals leaves them tired, moody and slower.» What does moody suggest? | Excited about dinner | *Cross or sad for no clear reason | Sleepy in bed | Full of energy and singing
test: Lacey snaps, «Mind your own, mardy». What does mardy mean? | Lost in the park | Happy and bouncy | *Moody and grumpy | Clean and tidy
test: «A threenager» is a jokey word. What does it mean? | *A defiant three-year-old acting like a moody teenager | A toddler who loves cake | A teenager who is three years older | A baby who sleeps all day
exam: Which best describes «moody weather»? | Silent and still, with no wind at all | Bright and windy with clear blue sky | Sunny all day, hot enough for the beach | *Dark, changing quickly and gloomy
